From e8f8dc91c5631aaf854feeb0eb30787439ce90e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/77] consensus: deploy OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S, on Ark-0 from
 height 32000

A buried deployment, p2mr_slhdsa128s, sets SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_SLHDSA128S
on blocks at or above its height where P2MR is active too.

- On the Ark-0 signet the height is a rule of that network,
  ARK0_SLHDSA128S_HEIGHT: 32000. It covers this opcode only. A
  static_assert keeps it above the height of the P2MR tripwire rules
  (30000), since leaf version 0xe0 must execute before the opcode can run
  in it. Once a build carrying it has left the network's own nodes, the
  height does not change.
- Another custom signet gets the rules from -signetslhdsa128s=<height>,
  which requires -signetchallenge and which Ark-0 refuses. A node refuses
  to start with it on any other chain, whatever its value.
- Regtest activates them at genesis unless
  -testactivationheight=p2mr_slhdsa128s@N says otherwise.
- Mainnet, testnet3, testnet4 and the default signet never activate them.

getdeploymentinfo reports the deployment, and a node where it is enabled
logs "P2MR SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s rules active from height N (leaf versions
0xc0, 0xe0)" at startup.
